# Figure manifest: which generated figure feeds which name used in main.tex.
#
# Format:  <stable-name>  <TAB or spaces>  <source glob>
#
# The stable name on the left is what main.tex cites with \includegraphics.
# The glob on the right may be date-stamped; refresh-figures.sh picks the
# NEWEST match and copies it to the stable name. That indirection is the
# whole point: analysis runs and re-exported drawings can keep changing their
# filenames, while the manuscript keeps citing one unchanging name.
#
# Globs are resolved against the source roots listed in refresh-figures.sh.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment 1 — beam degradation along the path
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setup drawing (Photoshop source alongside the export).
eod-setup-beam-degradation.png    EOD_exp_1.png

# Measured results, from the moving-EOD1 stage sweep (MAR_3 dataset).
eod-beam-quality.png              beam_quality_plot.png
eod-beam-xcorr.png                beam_quality_xcorr.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment 2 — beam deflection against drive voltage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setup drawing (Photoshop source alongside the export). The source filename
# carries a typo, "delfection", which is why the glob does not read cleanly.
eod-setup-beam-deflection.png     EOD_exp_2_beam delfection.png
